{
  "title": "Fourier series",
  "hue": 205,
  "lede": "A Fourier series writes a repeating shape as a sum of sine and cosine waves whose frequencies are whole-number multiples of one base frequency. Add enough of them and they rebuild a square wave, a sawtooth, a heartbeat, or any other periodic signal.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "kind": "experience",
      "heading": "Add circles, watch the wave",
      "body": "<style>\n.fsc{font-family:var(--ow-font);color:var(--ow-fg);-webkit-user-select:none;user-select:none;-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}\n.fsc .stagebox{position:relative}\n.fsc canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:300px}\n.fsc .legend{position:absolute;top:6px;right:4px;display:flex;gap:14px;font-size:12px;color:var(--ow-muted);pointer-events:none}\n.fsc .legend i{display:inline-block;width:18px;height:0;border-top:2.5px solid var(--ow-accent);vertical-align:middle;margin-right:6px}\n.fsc .legend i.t{border-top:1.5px dashed var(--ow-muted)}\n.fsc .panel{margin-top:14px;background:var(--ow-panel);border:1px solid var(--ow-line);border-radius:16px;padding:14px 18px 16px}\n.fsc .row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:12px 18px}\n.fsc .row+.row{margin-top:14px}\n.fsc .seg{display:inline-flex;gap:2px;padding:3px;border-radius:999px;border:1px solid var(--ow-line)}\n.fsc .seg button,.fsc .play{appearance:none;border:0;background:transparent;color:var(--ow-muted);font-size:14px;line-height:20px;padding:7px 14px;border-radius:999px;cursor:pointer;display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;transition:background .15s,color .15s}\n.fsc .seg button:hover{color:var(--ow-fg)}\n.fsc .seg button[aria-pressed=\"true\"]{background:var(--ow-accent);color:var(--ow-accent-ink)}\n.fsc .seg svg{width:22px;height:12px;flex:none}\n.fsc .play{border:1px solid var(--ow-line);color:var(--ow-fg);padding:7px 14px}\n.fsc .play:hover{border-color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.fsc button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ow-accent);outline-offset:2px}\n.fsc input[type=range]:focus-visible{outline:none}\n.fsc input[type=range]:focus-visible::-webkit-slider-thumb{box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--ow-accent),0 0 0 6px var(--ow-line)}\n.fsc input[type=range]:focus-visible::-moz-range-thumb{box-shadow:0 0 0 5px var(--ow-line)}\n.fsc .short{display:none}\n.fsc .stats{margin-left:auto;display:flex;gap:18px;white-space:nowrap;font-size:12px;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.fsc .stats b{display:block;font:600 17px/1.2 var(--ow-mono);color:var(--ow-fg);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.fsc .n{font:600 30px/1 var(--ow-mono);min-width:2.2ch;text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:var(--ow-accent)}\n.fsc .nl{font-size:13px;color:var(--ow-muted);line-height:1.2;width:4.6em}\n.fsc input[type=range]{flex:1 1 200px;min-width:0;height:28px;margin:0;background:transparent;-webkit-appearance:none;appearance:none;cursor:pointer;touch-action:pan-y}\n.fsc input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-runnable-track{height:6px;border-radius:3px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--ow-accent) var(--p,0%),var(--ow-line) var(--p,0%))}\n.fsc input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-thumb{-webkit-appearance:none;width:24px;height:24px;margin-top:-9px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ow-accent);border:3px solid var(--ow-panel);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--ow-accent)}\n.fsc input[type=range]::-moz-range-track{height:6px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--ow-line)}\n.fsc input[type=range]::-moz-range-progress{height:6px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--ow-accent)}\n.fsc input[type=range]::-moz-range-thumb{width:18px;height:18px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ow-accent);border:3px solid var(--ow-panel)}\n.fsc .hint{font-size:13px;color:var(--ow-muted);margin:10px 2px 0;min-height:20px}\n.fsc .row.sl{flex-wrap:nowrap}\n@media (max-width:560px){.fsc .seg{width:100%}.fsc .seg button{flex:1;justify-content:center;padding:7px 6px;gap:6px}.fsc .stats{order:2;margin-left:0;flex:1}.fsc .play{order:3}.fsc .panel{padding:12px 14px 14px}.fsc .legend{display:none}.fsc .long{display:none}.fsc .short{display:inline}.fsc .hint{margin-top:8px}}\n</style>\n<div class=\"fsc\">\n  <div class=\"stagebox\">\n    <canvas aria-label=\"A chain of rotating circles whose tip traces a wave that scrolls to the right\"></canvas>\n    <div class=\"legend\"><span><i></i>sum of circles</span><span><i class=\"t\"></i>target shape</span></div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"panel\">\n    <div class=\"row\">\n      <div class=\"seg\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Target shape\">\n        <button type=\"button\" data-s=\"square\" aria-pressed=\"true\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 22 12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M1 10V2h10v8h10V2\"/></svg>Square</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" data-s=\"saw\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 22 12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M1 10L11 2v8L21 2v8\"/></svg>Sawtooth</button>\n        <button type=\"button\" data-s=\"tri\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 22 12\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\"><path d=\"M1 10L6 2l5 8 5-8 5 8\"/></svg>Triangle</button>\n      </div>\n      <button type=\"button\" class=\"play\" aria-label=\"Pause\"></button>\n      <div class=\"stats\" aria-live=\"polite\">\n        <div><span class=\"long\">average error</span><span class=\"short\">error</span><b class=\"err\">0.00</b></div>\n        <div><span class=\"long\">overshoot at a jump</span><span class=\"short\">overshoot</span><b class=\"ovs\">0%</b></div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"row sl\">\n      <span class=\"n\">1</span><span class=\"nl\">circle<br>(term)</span>\n      <input type=\"range\" min=\"1\" max=\"50\" step=\"1\" value=\"1\" aria-label=\"Number of terms (circles)\">\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"hint\"></p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var root = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;\n  var cv = root.querySelector(\"canvas\"), cx = cv.getContext(\"2d\");\n  var slider = root.querySelector(\"input\"), nEl = root.querySelector(\".n\"), nl = root.querySelector(\".nl\");\n  var errEl = root.querySelector(\".err\"), ovsEl = root.querySelector(\".ovs\"), hint = root.querySelector(\".hint\");\n  var playBtn = root.querySelector(\".play\"), segs = root.querySelectorAll(\".seg button\");\n  var MAXN = 50, TAU = Math.PI * 2, PERIOD_S = 5;\n  var shape = \"square\", N = 1, t = 0.9, paused = false, visible = true;\n  var weight = new Float32Array(MAXN); weight[0] = 1;\n  var reduce = matchMedia(\"(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\");\n  var col = {}, W = 0, H = 0, dpr = 1;\n\n  // n-th nonzero term (0-based) of each target: [angular frequency, amplitude]\n  function term(s, i) {\n    if (s === \"square\") { var k = 2 * i + 1; return [k, 4 / (Math.PI * k)]; }\n    if (s === \"saw\") { var m = i + 1; return [m, (m % 2 ? 2 : -2) / (Math.PI * m)]; }\n    var q = 2 * i + 1; return [q, (i % 2 ? -8 : 8) / (Math.PI * Math.PI * q * q)];\n  }\n  function target(s, x) {\n    x = ((x % TAU) + TAU) % TAU;\n    if (s === \"square\") return x < Math.PI ? 1 : -1;\n    if (s === \"saw\") return x < Math.PI ? x / Math.PI : x / Math.PI - 2;\n    return x < Math.PI / 2 ? x * 2 / Math.PI : x < 1.5 * Math.PI ? 2 - x * 2 / Math.PI : x * 2 / Math.PI - 4;\n  }\n  var K = new Float32Array(MAXN), A = new Float32Array(MAXN), X = new Float32Array(MAXN);\n  // Only a circle's height draws the wave, so each circle may turn either way. Pick the turn\n  // directions that keep the chain compact (a fixed seeded search), so it never leaves its box.\n  var turns = {}, REACH = 1.3;\n  (function () {\n    var seed = 7; function rnd() { seed = (seed * 16807) % 2147483647; return seed / 2147483647; }\n    [\"square\", \"saw\", \"tri\"].forEach(function (s) {\n      var k = [], a = []; for (var i = 0; i < MAXN; i++) { var p = term(s, i); k.push(p[0]); a.push(Math.abs(p[1])); }\n      var best = null, bestR = 1e9;\n      for (var trial = 0; trial < 160; trial++) {\n        var sg = [1]; for (var i2 = 1; i2 < MAXN; i2++) sg.push(trial === 0 ? 1 : rnd() < 0.5 ? 1 : -1);\n        var r = 0;\n        [6, 15, 30, 50].forEach(function (n) {\n          for (var q = 0; q < 96; q++) {\n            var t = q / 96 * TAU, x = 0; for (var j = 0; j < n; j++) x += sg[j] * a[j] * Math.cos(k[j] * t);\n            r = Math.max(r, Math.abs(x));\n          }\n        });\n        if (r < bestR) { bestR = r; best = sg; }\n      }\n      turns[s] = best; REACH = Math.max(REACH, bestR);\n    });\n  })();\n  function loadShape() { for (var i = 0; i < MAXN; i++) { var p = term(shape, i); K[i] = p[0]; A[i] = p[1]; X[i] = turns[shape][i] * Math.abs(p[1]); } }\n\n  function stats() {\n    var M = 3000, max = -9, se = 0;\n    for (var j = 0; j < M; j++) {\n      var x = (j + 0.5) / M * TAU, s = 0;\n      for (var i = 0; i < N; i++) s += A[i] * Math.sin(K[i] * x);\n      if (s > max) max = s;\n      var d = s - target(shape, x); se += d * d;\n    }\n    errEl.textContent = Math.sqrt(se / M).toFixed(3);\n    if (shape === \"tri\") ovsEl.textContent = \"no jumps\";\n    else ovsEl.textContent = (Math.max(0, max - 1) / 2 * 100).toFixed(1) + \"%\";\n    nEl.textContent = N;\n    nl.innerHTML = N === 1 ? \"circle<br>(term)\" : \"circles<br>(terms)\";\n    slider.style.setProperty(\"--p\", ((N - 1) / (MAXN - 1) * 100) + \"%\");\n    slider.setAttribute(\"aria-valuetext\", N + (N === 1 ? \" term\" : \" terms\"));\n    var ks = []; for (var i = 0; i < Math.min(N, 4); i++) ks.push(K[i]);\n    hint.textContent = N === 1 ? \"One circle draws a plain sine wave. Drag the slider to add circles.\"\n      : \"Frequencies \" + ks.join(\", \") + (N > 4 ? \", ... \" + K[N - 1] : \"\") + \" times the first.\"\n        + (shape === \"tri\" ? \" No jumps, so the fit gets close fast.\" : N >= 12 ? \" The error keeps falling, the overshoot at the jump does not.\" : \"\");\n  }\n\n  function readColors() {\n    var cs = getComputedStyle(root);\n    [\"--ow-fg\", \"--ow-muted\", \"--ow-accent\", \"--ow-line\"].forEach(function (v) { col[v] = cs.getPropertyValue(v).trim(); });\n  }\n  function layout() {\n    var w = Math.round(root.clientWidth); if (!w) return;\n    var h = Math.round(Math.max(170, Math.min(380, w * 0.36)));\n    dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 3);\n    if (w === W && h === H && cv.width === Math.round(w * dpr)) return;\n    W = w; H = h;\n    cv.style.height = h + \"px\";\n    cv.width = Math.round(w * dpr); cv.height = Math.round(h * dpr);\n    readColors(); draw();\n  }\n\n  function draw() {\n    if (!W) return;\n    cx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0);\n    cx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n    var unit = Math.min(H * 0.29, W * (W < 600 ? 0.155 : 0.13)), cy = H / 2;\n    var ox = unit * REACH + (W > 600 ? W * 0.03 : 6);\n    var x0 = ox + unit * REACH + (W > 600 ? 28 : 10), waveW = W - x0;\n    var pxPerRad = Math.max(22, Math.min(58, waveW / (TAU * 2.1)));\n    // axis\n    cx.globalAlpha = 1; cx.strokeStyle = col[\"--ow-line\"]; cx.lineWidth = 1;\n    cx.beginPath(); cx.moveTo(x0, cy); cx.lineTo(W, cy); cx.stroke();\n    // target\n    cx.setLineDash([4, 5]); cx.strokeStyle = col[\"--ow-muted\"]; cx.lineWidth = 1.4; cx.globalAlpha = 0.9;\n    cx.beginPath();\n    for (var d = 0; d <= waveW; d += 1) { var y = cy - unit * target(shape, t - d / pxPerRad); d ? cx.lineTo(x0 + d, y) : cx.moveTo(x0 + d, y); }\n    cx.stroke(); cx.setLineDash([]);\n    // wave, analytic so a change of N redraws the whole curve at once\n    var used = 0; for (var i = 0; i < MAXN; i++) if (weight[i] > 0.001) used = i + 1;\n    cx.globalAlpha = 1; cx.strokeStyle = col[\"--ow-accent\"]; cx.lineWidth = 2.5; cx.lineJoin = \"round\";\n    cx.beginPath();\n    for (var d2 = 0; d2 <= waveW; d2 += 0.75) {\n      var tt = t - d2 / pxPerRad, s = 0;\n      for (var j = 0; j < used; j++) s += weight[j] * A[j] * Math.sin(K[j] * tt);\n      var yy = cy - unit * s; d2 ? cx.lineTo(x0 + d2, yy) : cx.moveTo(x0 + d2, yy);\n    }\n    cx.stroke();\n    // fade the far right to transparent\n    var fw = Math.min(90, waveW * 0.25);\n    var g = cx.createLinearGradient(W - fw, 0, W, 0); g.addColorStop(0, \"rgba(0,0,0,0)\"); g.addColorStop(1, \"rgba(0,0,0,1)\");\n    cx.globalCompositeOperation = \"destination-out\"; cx.fillStyle = g; cx.fillRect(W - fw, 0, fw, H); cx.globalCompositeOperation = \"source-over\";\n    // epicycles\n    var px = ox, py = cy;\n    for (var k = 0; k < used; k++) {\n      var ww = weight[k] * unit, ang = K[k] * t, nx = px + ww * X[k] * Math.cos(ang), ny = py - ww * A[k] * Math.sin(ang), ar = Math.abs(ww * A[k]);\n      if (ar > 0.4) {\n        cx.globalAlpha = k === 0 ? 0.38 : 0.26; cx.strokeStyle = col[\"--ow-fg\"]; cx.lineWidth = 1;\n        cx.beginPath(); cx.arc(px, py, ar, 0, TAU); cx.stroke();\n      }\n      cx.globalAlpha = 0.85; cx.lineWidth = k === 0 ? 1.6 : 1.2;\n      cx.beginPath(); cx.moveTo(px, py); cx.lineTo(nx, ny); cx.stroke();\n      if (ar > 3) { cx.globalAlpha = 0.9; cx.fillStyle = col[\"--ow-fg\"]; cx.beginPath(); cx.arc(px, py, 1.6, 0, TAU); cx.fill(); }\n      px = nx; py = ny;\n    }\n    // connector and pen\n    cx.globalAlpha = 0.7; cx.strokeStyle = col[\"--ow-muted\"]; cx.lineWidth = 1; cx.setLineDash([2, 4]);\n    cx.beginPath(); cx.moveTo(px, py); cx.lineTo(x0, py); cx.stroke(); cx.setLineDash([]);\n    cx.globalAlpha = 1; cx.fillStyle = col[\"--ow-accent\"];\n    cx.beginPath(); cx.arc(px, py, 4.5, 0, TAU); cx.fill();\n    cx.beginPath(); cx.arc(x0, py, 3, 0, TAU); cx.fill();\n  }\n\n  var last = 0, raf = 0;\n  function settle(dt) {\n    var moving = false, a = reduce.matches ? 1 : 1 - Math.exp(-dt / 0.09);\n    for (var i = 0; i < MAXN; i++) {\n      var goal = i < N ? 1 : 0, w = weight[i] + (goal - weight[i]) * a;\n      if (Math.abs(goal - w) < 0.002) w = goal; else moving = true;\n      weight[i] = w;\n    }\n    return moving;\n  }\n  function frame(now) {\n    raf = 0;\n    var dt = last ? Math.min(0.05, (now - last) / 1000) : 0; last = now;\n    var running = !paused && !reduce.matches && visible;\n    if (running) t += dt * TAU / PERIOD_S;\n    var moving = settle(dt);\n    draw();\n    if (running || moving) raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame); else last = 0;\n  }\n  function kick() { if (!raf) raf = requestAnimationFrame(frame); }\n\n  function syncPlay() {\n    if (reduce.matches) { playBtn.innerHTML = '<svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 14 14\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M2 2l6 5-6 5zM9 2h2.5v10H9z\"/></svg>Step'; playBtn.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", \"Step forward\"); }\n    else if (paused) { playBtn.innerHTML = '<svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 14 14\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 1.5l9 5.5-9 5.5z\"/></svg>Play'; playBtn.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", \"Play\"); }\n    else { playBtn.innerHTML = '<svg width=\"14\" height=\"14\" viewBox=\"0 0 14 14\" fill=\"currentColor\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M3 2h3v10H3zM8 2h3v10H8z\"/></svg>Pause'; playBtn.setAttribute(\"aria-label\", \"Pause\"); }\n  }\n  playBtn.addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n    if (reduce.matches) { t += TAU / 16; draw(); return; }\n    paused = !paused; syncPlay(); kick();\n  });\n  reduce.addEventListener && reduce.addEventListener(\"change\", function () { syncPlay(); kick(); });\n  slider.addEventListener(\"input\", function () { N = +slider.value; stats(); kick(); });\n  segs.forEach(function (b) {\n    b.addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n      shape = b.dataset.s; segs.forEach(function (o) { o.setAttribute(\"aria-pressed\", String(o === b)); });\n      loadShape(); stats(); kick(); draw();\n    });\n  });\n  if (window.IntersectionObserver) new IntersectionObserver(function (e) { visible = e[0].isIntersecting; kick(); }).observe(cv);\n  document.addEventListener(\"visibilitychange\", function () { visible = !document.hidden; kick(); });\n  new ResizeObserver(layout).observe(root);\n  loadShape(); stats(); syncPlay(); layout(); kick();\n})();\n</script>"
    },
    {
      "heading": "What it is",
      "body": "Every circle on the cover is one term of a Fourier series. It spins at a fixed speed, and the height of its tip over time is a sine wave. Stack circles tip to tail and the height of the last tip is the sum of all their sine waves. With the right sizes and speeds, that sum can trace almost any shape that repeats.\n\nThat is the whole idea: a periodic function becomes a list of plain waves, each with its own size. The payoff is that sines and cosines are simple to work with, so a hard problem about the shape can be split into many easy problems about waves [1]. A square wave that jumps between +1 and -1, for example, is an infinite sum of sine waves [2], and every extra term brings the sum closer to it [3].\n\nThe waves in the list are the [[Harmonic|harmonics]] of the shape: the first repeats once per period, the second twice, the third three times, and so on.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_series",
          "title": "Fourier series (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "By expressing a function as a sum of sines and cosines, many problems involving the function become easier to analyze because trigonometric functions are well understood."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Square_wave_(waveform)",
          "title": "Square wave (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "an ideal square wave with an amplitude of 1 can be represented as an infinite sum of sinusoidal waves"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_series",
          "title": "Fourier series (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "As more harmonics are added, the partial sums converge to the square wave."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The formula in plain words",
      "body": "Measure the period as one full turn (2π, about 6.28). The Fourier series of a shape f says:\n\nf(x) = a0 + a1·cos x + b1·sin x + a2·cos 2x + b2·sin 2x + a3·cos 3x + b3·sin 3x + ...\n\nIn words: a constant, plus a wave that fits once in the period, plus one that fits twice, plus one that fits three times, forever. The numbers a1, b1, a2, b2 and so on are the **coefficients**. They say how much of each harmonic the shape contains.\n\nEach coefficient comes from one integral: multiply the shape by that harmonic and add up the product over one period [1]. In averaging terms:\n\n- a0 is the average height of the shape.\n- bn is twice the average of f(x)·sin(nx).\n- an is twice the average of f(x)·cos(nx).\n\nFor a square wave that sits at +1 for half a period and -1 for the other half, every cosine coefficient and every even harmonic come out as zero. Only the odd sines survive [2]:\n\nsquare(x) = (4/π) · ( sin x + sin 3x / 3 + sin 5x / 5 + sin 7x / 7 + ... )\n\nThat is the cover's square setting: circles with radii 4/π, 4/3π, 4/5π, spinning 1, 3 and 5 times as fast as the first.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_series",
          "title": "Fourier series (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The coefficients of the Fourier series are determined by integrals of the function multiplied by trigonometric functions"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Square_wave_(waveform)",
          "title": "Square wave (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The ideal square wave contains only components of odd-integer harmonic frequencies"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "experience",
      "heading": "Build it yourself",
      "body": "<style>\n.fsb{font-family:var(--ow-font);color:var(--ow-fg);-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}\n.fsb .card{background:var(--ow-panel);border:1px solid var(--ow-line);border-radius:16px;padding:14px 16px 16px}\n.fsb canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:210px}\n.fsb .eq{font:14px/1.5 var(--ow-mono);color:var(--ow-muted);margin:10px 2px 12px;min-height:21px;overflow-wrap:anywhere}\n.fsb .eq span{white-space:nowrap}\n.fsb .eq b{color:var(--ow-accent);font-weight:600}\n.fsb .rows{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 1fr auto;gap:4px 14px;align-items:center}\n.fsb label{font:14px var(--ow-mono);color:var(--ow-muted);white-space:nowrap;transition:color .15s}\n.fsb .on label,.fsb label.on{color:var(--ow-fg)}\n.fsb output{font:600 14px var(--ow-mono);min-width:5ch;text-align:right;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.fsb input[type=range]{width:100%;min-width:0;height:30px;margin:0;background:transparent;-webkit-appearance:none;appearance:none;cursor:pointer;touch-action:pan-y}\n.fsb input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-runnable-track{height:6px;border-radius:3px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--ow-line) calc(50% - 1px),var(--ow-muted) calc(50% - 1px),var(--ow-muted) calc(50% + 1px),var(--ow-line) calc(50% + 1px))}\n.fsb input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-thumb{-webkit-appearance:none;width:22px;height:22px;margin-top:-8px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ow-accent);border:3px solid var(--ow-panel);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--ow-accent)}\n.fsb input[type=range]::-moz-range-track{height:6px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--ow-line)}\n.fsb input[type=range]::-moz-range-thumb{width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ow-accent);border:3px solid var(--ow-panel)}\n.fsb .presets{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-top:14px;align-items:center}\n.fsb .presets span{font-size:13px;color:var(--ow-muted);margin-right:4px}\n.fsb button{appearance:none;border:1px solid var(--ow-line);background:transparent;color:var(--ow-fg);font-size:14px;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:999px;cursor:pointer;transition:background .15s,color .15s,border-color .15s}\n.fsb button:hover{border-color:var(--ow-accent)}\n.fsb button.primary{background:var(--ow-accent);border-color:var(--ow-accent);color:var(--ow-accent-ink)}\n.fsb input[type=range]:focus-visible{outline:none}\n.fsb input[type=range]:focus-visible::-webkit-slider-thumb{box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--ow-accent),0 0 0 6px var(--ow-line)}\n.fsb button:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ow-accent);outline-offset:2px}\n</style>\n<div class=\"fsb\"><div class=\"card\">\n  <canvas aria-label=\"Five sine harmonics drawn faintly, and their sum drawn bold\"></canvas>\n  <div class=\"eq\" aria-live=\"polite\"></div>\n  <div class=\"rows\"></div>\n  <div class=\"presets\"><span>Try:</span>\n    <button type=\"button\" class=\"primary\" data-p=\"1,0,0.3333,0,0.2\">Square recipe</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-p=\"1,-0.5,0.3333,-0.25,0.2\">Sawtooth recipe</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-p=\"1,0,-0.1111,0,0.04\">Triangle recipe</button>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-p=\"1,0,0,0,0\">Reset</button>\n  </div>\n</div></div>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var root = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;\n  var cv = root.querySelector(\"canvas\"), cx = cv.getContext(\"2d\"), eq = root.querySelector(\".eq\"), rows = root.querySelector(\".rows\");\n  var TAU = Math.PI * 2, amp = [1, 0, 0, 0, 0], shown = amp.slice(), focus = -1, col = {}, W = 0, H = 0, dpr = 1, scale = 1.2;\n  var reduce = matchMedia(\"(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)\");\n  var names = [\"sin x\", \"sin 2x\", \"sin 3x\", \"sin 4x\", \"sin 5x\"], inputs = [], outs = [], labels = [];\n  names.forEach(function (n, i) {\n    var id = \"fsb-\" + i + \"-\" + Math.random().toString(36).slice(2, 7);\n    var l = document.createElement(\"label\"); l.htmlFor = id; l.textContent = n;\n    var r = document.createElement(\"input\"); r.type = \"range\"; r.id = id; r.min = -1; r.max = 1; r.step = 0.01; r.value = amp[i];\n    var o = document.createElement(\"output\"); o.htmlFor = id;\n    rows.append(l, r, o); inputs.push(r); outs.push(o); labels.push(l);\n    r.addEventListener(\"input\", function () { amp[i] = +r.value; shown[i] = amp[i]; sync(); draw(); });\n    [\"pointerenter\", \"focus\"].forEach(function (e) { r.addEventListener(e, function () { focus = i; hl(); draw(); }); });\n    [\"pointerleave\", \"blur\"].forEach(function (e) { r.addEventListener(e, function () { if (focus === i && document.activeElement !== r) { focus = -1; hl(); draw(); } }); });\n  });\n  function hl() { labels.forEach(function (l, i) { l.classList.toggle(\"on\", i === focus); }); }\n  function fmt(v) { return (v < 0 ? \"−\" : \"\") + Math.abs(v).toFixed(2); }\n  function sync() {\n    var parts = [];\n    for (var i = 0; i < 5; i++) {\n      outs[i].textContent = fmt(shown[i]);\n      if (Math.abs(shown[i]) >= 0.005) parts.push((parts.length ? (shown[i] < 0 ? \" − \" : \" + \") : (shown[i] < 0 ? \"−\" : \"\")) + \"<span>\" + Math.abs(shown[i]).toFixed(2) + \"·\" + names[i] + \"</span>\");\n    }\n    eq.innerHTML = \"<b>sum</b> = \" + (parts.length ? parts.join(\"\") : \"0\");\n  }\n  function readColors() { var cs = getComputedStyle(root); [\"--ow-fg\", \"--ow-muted\", \"--ow-accent\", \"--ow-line\"].forEach(function (v) { col[v] = cs.getPropertyValue(v).trim(); }); }\n  function layout() {\n    var w = Math.round(cv.clientWidth), h = 210; if (!w) return;\n    dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 3);\n    if (w === W && cv.width === Math.round(w * dpr)) return;\n    W = w; H = h; cv.width = Math.round(w * dpr); cv.height = Math.round(h * dpr); readColors(); draw();\n  }\n  function sum(x) { var s = 0; for (var i = 0; i < 5; i++) s += shown[i] * Math.sin((i + 1) * x); return s; }\n  function draw() {\n    if (!W) return;\n    var max = 0.5; for (var j = 0; j <= 400; j++) max = Math.max(max, Math.abs(sum(j / 400 * TAU * 2)));\n    for (var i = 0; i < 5; i++) max = Math.max(max, Math.abs(shown[i]));\n    scale = max * 1.12;\n    cx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0); cx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n    var cy = H / 2, u = (H / 2 - 8) / scale, periods = 2;\n    cx.strokeStyle = col[\"--ow-line\"]; cx.lineWidth = 1; cx.globalAlpha = 1;\n    cx.beginPath(); cx.moveTo(0, cy); cx.lineTo(W, cy); cx.moveTo(W / 2, 6); cx.lineTo(W / 2, H - 6); cx.stroke();\n    cx.fillStyle = col[\"--ow-muted\"]; cx.font = \"12px \" + getComputedStyle(root).getPropertyValue(\"--ow-mono\");\n    cx.fillText(\"one period\", 6, H - 8); cx.fillText(\"the next\", W / 2 + 6, H - 8);\n    function curve(fn, color, lw, alpha) {\n      cx.strokeStyle = color; cx.lineWidth = lw; cx.globalAlpha = alpha; cx.lineJoin = \"round\"; cx.beginPath();\n      for (var p = 0; p <= W; p += 1) { var y = cy - u * fn(p / W * TAU * periods); p ? cx.lineTo(p, y) : cx.moveTo(p, y); }\n      cx.stroke();\n    }\n    for (var k = 0; k < 5; k++) {\n      if (Math.abs(shown[k]) < 0.005) continue;\n      (function (k) { curve(function (x) { return shown[k] * Math.sin((k + 1) * x); }, col[k === focus ? \"--ow-fg\" : \"--ow-muted\"], k === focus ? 1.8 : 1.2, k === focus ? 0.85 : 0.45); })(k);\n    }\n    curve(sum, col[\"--ow-accent\"], 3, 1);\n    cx.globalAlpha = 1;\n  }\n  var anim = 0;\n  function tween(to) {\n    cancelAnimationFrame(anim);\n    to.forEach(function (v, i) { amp[i] = v; inputs[i].value = v; });\n    if (reduce.matches) { shown = to.slice(); sync(); draw(); return; }\n    var from = shown.slice(), t0 = performance.now();\n    (function step(now) {\n      var p = Math.min(1, (now - t0) / 420), e = 1 - Math.pow(1 - p, 3);\n      for (var i = 0; i < 5; i++) shown[i] = from[i] + (to[i] - from[i]) * e;\n      sync(); draw(); if (p < 1) anim = requestAnimationFrame(step);\n    })(t0);\n  }\n  root.querySelectorAll(\"button\").forEach(function (b) {\n    b.addEventListener(\"click\", function () {\n      root.querySelectorAll(\"button\").forEach(function (o) { o.classList.toggle(\"primary\", o === b); });\n      tween(b.dataset.p.split(\",\").map(Number));\n    });\n  });\n  new ResizeObserver(layout).observe(cv);\n  sync(); layout();\n})();\n</script>"
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why sines and cosines work",
      "body": "Multiply sin x by sin 3x and average the result over a full period. You get exactly zero. For part of the period the two waves have the same sign and the product is positive; for the rest they disagree and it is negative, and the two parts cancel [1]. The same happens for any two different harmonics, and for any sine paired with any cosine [2]. Functions with this property are called **orthogonal**, because the averaged product plays the role that the dot product plays for arrows: zero means perpendicular [3].\n\nThis is what makes the recipe above work. Multiply the whole series by sin 3x and average: every term cancels to zero except the sin 3x term itself. So each coefficient can be measured on its own, as if the other harmonics were not there, and adding a new term never changes the ones already found.\n\nIt also means that stopping after N harmonics gives the best fit of that size. No other choice of the same waves has a smaller average squared error [4]. The \"average error\" readout on the cover falls every time you add a circle for this reason.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_series",
          "title": "Fourier series (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The integral of sine, cosine and their product is zero (green and red areas are equal, and cancel out)"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orthogonal_functions",
          "title": "Orthogonal functions (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "and the integral of the product of the two sine functions vanishes."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orthogonal_functions",
          "title": "Orthogonal functions (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Conceptually, the above integral is the equivalent of a vector dot product"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_series",
          "title": "Fourier series (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "is the unique best trigonometric polynomial of degree"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "The overshoot that never goes away",
      "body": "Set the cover to a square wave and slide up to 50 circles. The curve hugs the flat parts ever more tightly, but right beside each jump it still overshoots, by about 9% of the jump. More terms squeeze the wiggle closer to the jump; they do not make it smaller [1]. This is the [[Gibbs phenomenon]].\n\nIt happens wherever the shape has a jump, which is why the triangle setting on the cover shows none: a triangle bends but never breaks. It is not a sign that the series is wrong: the wiggle gets thinner, so the error it adds on average still shrinks toward zero [4].\n\nThe effect is named after the physicist J. Willard Gibbs, who described it in 1899, but Henry Wilbraham had noticed and analyzed it in 1848 [2]. It became famous through Albert Michelson's mechanical harmonic analyzer; a widely told story says he thought the wiggle was a flaw in his machine [3].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibbs_phenomenon",
          "title": "Gibbs phenomenon (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "As more sinusoids are used, this approximation error approaches a limit of about 9% of the jump"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibbs_phenomenon",
          "title": "Gibbs phenomenon (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The Gibbs phenomenon was first noticed and analyzed by Henry Wilbraham in an 1848 paper."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibbs_phenomenon",
          "title": "Gibbs phenomenon (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Michelson was convinced that the overshoot was caused by errors in the machine."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibbs_phenomenon",
          "title": "Gibbs phenomenon (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "and this oscillation does not disappear but gets closer to the point so that the integral of the oscillation approaches zero."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Fourier and the heat equation",
      "body": "Joseph Fourier (1768 to 1830) was a French mathematician who also served as scientific adviser on Napoleon's expedition to Egypt [1]. He was trying to predict how heat spreads through a solid, the problem now written as the [[Heat equation]]. Solutions were known only when the starting heat was laid out as a single sine or cosine wave [2].\n\nHis idea was to break any starting temperature into sine and cosine waves, solve for each wave separately, and add the answers back up [2]. Each wave just fades over time, and adding the fading waves back up shows the temperature gradually evening out [4].\n\nHe read the work to the Paris Institute on 21 December 1807. Lagrange and Laplace objected to the claim that such arbitrary functions could be written as trigonometric series [3], and Fourier published the full theory in 1822.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Fourier",
          "title": "Joseph Fourier (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Fourier accompanied Napoleon Bonaparte on his Egyptian expedition in 1798, as scientific adviser"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_series",
          "title": "Fourier series (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Fourier's idea was to model a complicated heat source as a superposition"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://mathshistory.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Fourier/",
          "title": "Joseph Fourier biography (MacTutor, University of St Andrews)",
          "quote": "The first objection, made by Lagrange and Laplace in 1808"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heat_equation",
          "title": "Heat equation (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Solutions of the heat equation are characterized by a gradual smoothing of the initial temperature distribution"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Where it is used today",
      "body": "The same move, splitting a signal into frequencies, runs through modern engineering:\n\n| Where | What the frequencies buy |\n|---|---|\n| Images | [[JPEG]] cuts each photo into 8 by 8 blocks, turns each block into cosine coefficients, and throws away the fine ones the eye barely sees [1] |\n| Audio | [[MP3]] and AAC store sound as coefficients of a close cousin, the modified discrete cosine transform [2] |\n| Signal processing | Filters, equalizers, radio and noise removal all work on frequency coefficients; the [[Discrete cosine transform]] alone is the most widely used transform in the field [3] |\n| Differential equations | Heat flow, vibrating strings and other linear equations with constant coefficients split into one easy equation per harmonic [4] |\n\nA Fourier series needs a shape that repeats. For signals that do not repeat, the [[Fourier transform]] does the same job with a continuous range of frequencies, and computers use the [[Fast Fourier transform]] to compute it quickly.\n\nTry it below: draw any curve and see how few harmonics it takes to capture its outline. The bars show how strong each harmonic is. Smooth drawings put nearly all their weight in the first few bars; jagged ones need many more. That gap is the reason compression works.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/JPEG",
          "title": "JPEG (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "JPEG uses a lossy form of compression based on the discrete cosine transform (DCT)."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MP3",
          "title": "MP3 (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The MDCT later became a core part of the MP3 algorithm."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discrete_cosine_transform",
          "title": "Discrete cosine transform (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "The DCT is the most widely used transformation technique in signal processing"
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_series",
          "title": "Fourier series (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "especially those involving linear differential equations with constant coefficients, for which the eigensolutions are sinusoids"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "kind": "experience",
      "heading": "Draw your own curve",
      "body": "<style>\n.fsd{font-family:var(--ow-font);color:var(--ow-fg);-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent}\n.fsd .card{background:var(--ow-panel);border:1px solid var(--ow-line);border-radius:16px;padding:14px 16px 16px}\n.fsd .pad{position:relative;border:1px dashed var(--ow-line);border-radius:12px}\n.fsd canvas.d{display:block;width:100%;height:240px;touch-action:none;cursor:crosshair;border-radius:10px}\n.fsd canvas.s{display:block;width:100%;height:64px;margin-top:6px}\n.fsd .tip{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:12px;text-align:center;font-size:14px;color:var(--ow-muted);pointer-events:none;transition:opacity .3s}\n.fsd .tip b{color:var(--ow-fg);font-weight:600}\n.fsd .row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;gap:10px 16px;margin-top:12px}\n.fsd .n{font:600 22px/1 var(--ow-mono);min-width:2ch;text-align:right;color:var(--ow-accent);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.fsd .nl{font-size:13px;color:var(--ow-muted);line-height:1.2}\n.fsd input[type=range]{flex:1 1 160px;min-width:0;height:30px;margin:0;background:transparent;-webkit-appearance:none;appearance:none;cursor:pointer;touch-action:pan-y}\n.fsd input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-runnable-track{height:6px;border-radius:3px;background:linear-gradient(90deg,var(--ow-accent) var(--p,0%),var(--ow-line) var(--p,0%))}\n.fsd input[type=range]::-webkit-slider-thumb{-webkit-appearance:none;width:22px;height:22px;margin-top:-8px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ow-accent);border:3px solid var(--ow-panel);box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--ow-accent)}\n.fsd input[type=range]::-moz-range-track{height:6px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--ow-line)}\n.fsd input[type=range]::-moz-range-progress{height:6px;border-radius:3px;background:var(--ow-accent)}\n.fsd input[type=range]::-moz-range-thumb{width:16px;height:16px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ow-accent);border:3px solid var(--ow-panel)}\n.fsd .err{font-size:12px;color:var(--ow-muted)}\n.fsd .err b{display:block;font:600 16px/1.2 var(--ow-mono);color:var(--ow-fg);font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}\n.fsd button{appearance:none;border:1px solid var(--ow-line);background:transparent;color:var(--ow-fg);font-size:14px;padding:6px 14px;border-radius:999px;cursor:pointer}\n.fsd button:hover{border-color:var(--ow-accent)}\n.fsd input[type=range]:focus-visible{outline:none}\n.fsd input[type=range]:focus-visible::-webkit-slider-thumb{box-shadow:0 0 0 1px var(--ow-accent),0 0 0 6px var(--ow-line)}\n.fsd button:focus-visible,.fsd canvas:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--ow-accent);outline-offset:2px}\n.fsd .legend{display:flex;gap:14px;font-size:12px;color:var(--ow-muted);margin-top:8px;flex-wrap:wrap}\n.fsd .legend i{display:inline-block;width:16px;height:0;vertical-align:middle;margin-right:6px}\n</style>\n<div class=\"fsd\"><div class=\"card\">\n  <div class=\"pad\">\n    <canvas class=\"d\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-label=\"Drawing area: draw one period of any curve from left to right. Press E for the example, C to clear.\"></canvas>\n    <div class=\"tip\"><b>Draw one period</b> of any curve, left to right</div>\n  </div>\n  <div class=\"legend\"><span><i style=\"border-top:5px solid var(--ow-muted);opacity:.4\"></i>your drawing</span><span><i style=\"border-top:2.5px solid var(--ow-accent)\"></i>sum of the first N harmonics</span><span><i style=\"border-top:6px solid var(--ow-accent);width:6px\"></i>how much of each harmonic</span></div>\n  <canvas class=\"s\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></canvas>\n  <div class=\"row\">\n    <span class=\"n\">5</span><span class=\"nl\">harmonics</span>\n    <input type=\"range\" min=\"1\" max=\"30\" step=\"1\" value=\"5\" aria-label=\"Number of harmonics used\">\n    <div class=\"err\">average error<b>0.000</b></div>\n    <button type=\"button\" data-a=\"ex\">Example</button><button type=\"button\" data-a=\"clear\">Clear</button>\n  </div>\n</div></div>\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var root = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;\n  var dc = root.querySelector(\"canvas.d\"), sc = root.querySelector(\"canvas.s\"), dx = dc.getContext(\"2d\"), sx = sc.getContext(\"2d\");\n  var tip = root.querySelector(\".tip\"), slider = root.querySelector(\"input\"), nEl = root.querySelector(\".n\"), errEl = root.querySelector(\".err b\");\n  var TAU = Math.PI * 2, M = 512, MAXN = 30, N = 5, col = {}, dpr = 1, W = 0, H = 240, SW = 0, SH = 64;\n  var y = new Float32Array(M), have = new Uint8Array(M), filled = new Float32Array(M), any = false;\n  var a = new Float32Array(MAXN + 1), b = new Float32Array(MAXN + 1), cosT = [], sinT = [];\n  for (var n = 0; n <= MAXN; n++) { var c = new Float32Array(M), s = new Float32Array(M); for (var j = 0; j < M; j++) { var x = (j + 0.5) / M * TAU; c[j] = Math.cos(n * x); s[j] = Math.sin(n * x); } cosT.push(c); sinT.push(s); }\n\n  function example() {\n    for (var j = 0; j < M; j++) {\n      var u = j / M, v;\n      if (u < 0.22) v = -0.55 + 1.6 * u;\n      else if (u < 0.3) v = -0.2 + 0.85 * Math.sin((u - 0.22) / 0.08 * Math.PI);\n      else if (u < 0.55) v = 0.55;\n      else if (u < 0.75) v = 0.55 - 1.2 * Math.pow((u - 0.55) / 0.2, 2);\n      else v = -0.65 + 0.12 * Math.sin((u - 0.75) * 40);\n      y[j] = v; have[j] = 1;\n    }\n    any = true; tip.style.opacity = 0; solve();\n  }\n  function clear() { have.fill(0); any = false; tip.style.opacity = 1; solve(); }\n\n  // Gaps between drawn bins are filled linearly, wrapping around: the shape is periodic.\n  function fill() {\n    var idx = []; for (var j = 0; j < M; j++) if (have[j]) idx.push(j);\n    if (!idx.length) return false;\n    for (var k = 0; k < idx.length; k++) {\n      var i0 = idx[k], i1 = idx[(k + 1) % idx.length], gap = ((i1 - i0 + M) % M) || M;\n      for (var g = 0; g < gap; g++) filled[(i0 + g) % M] = y[i0] + (y[i1] - y[i0]) * g / gap;\n    }\n    return true;\n  }\n  function solve() {\n    a.fill(0); b.fill(0);\n    if (fill()) {\n      for (var n = 0; n <= MAXN; n++) {\n        var sa = 0, sb = 0, c = cosT[n], s = sinT[n];\n        for (var j = 0; j < M; j++) { sa += filled[j] * c[j]; sb += filled[j] * s[j]; }\n        a[n] = (n ? 2 : 1) * sa / M; b[n] = 2 * sb / M;\n      }\n    }\n    draw();\n  }\n  function approx(j) { var v = a[0]; for (var n = 1; n <= N; n++) v += a[n] * cosT[n][j] + b[n] * sinT[n][j]; return v; }\n  function readColors() { var cs = getComputedStyle(root); [\"--ow-fg\", \"--ow-muted\", \"--ow-accent\", \"--ow-line\"].forEach(function (v) { col[v] = cs.getPropertyValue(v).trim(); }); }\n  function size(c, w, h) { c.width = Math.round(w * dpr); c.height = Math.round(h * dpr); }\n  function layout() {\n    var w = Math.round(dc.clientWidth); if (!w) return;\n    dpr = Math.min(window.devicePixelRatio || 1, 3);\n    if (w === W && dc.width === Math.round(w * dpr)) return;\n    W = w; SW = Math.round(sc.clientWidth); size(dc, W, H); size(sc, SW, SH); readColors(); draw();\n  }\n  function Y(v) { return H / 2 - v * (H / 2 - 16); }\n  function draw() {\n    if (!W) return;\n    dx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0); dx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);\n    dx.globalAlpha = 1; dx.strokeStyle = col[\"--ow-line\"]; dx.lineWidth = 1; dx.setLineDash([3, 5]);\n    dx.beginPath(); dx.moveTo(0, H / 2); dx.lineTo(W, H / 2); dx.stroke(); dx.setLineDash([]);\n    var err = 0;\n    if (any) {\n      dx.strokeStyle = col[\"--ow-muted\"]; dx.globalAlpha = 0.32; dx.lineWidth = 7; dx.lineCap = \"round\"; dx.lineJoin = \"round\";\n      dx.beginPath(); for (var j = 0; j < M; j++) { var px = (j + 0.5) / M * W; j ? dx.lineTo(px, Y(filled[j])) : dx.moveTo(px, Y(filled[j])); } dx.stroke();\n      dx.globalAlpha = 1; dx.strokeStyle = col[\"--ow-accent\"]; dx.lineWidth = 2.5;\n      dx.beginPath(); for (var k = 0; k < M; k++) { var v = approx(k), p2 = (k + 0.5) / M * W; err += (v - filled[k]) * (v - filled[k]); k ? dx.lineTo(p2, Y(v)) : dx.moveTo(p2, Y(v)); } dx.stroke();\n      err = Math.sqrt(err / M);\n    }\n    errEl.textContent = any ? err.toFixed(3) : \"–\";\n    nEl.textContent = N; slider.style.setProperty(\"--p\", ((N - 1) / (MAXN - 1) * 100) + \"%\");\n    slider.setAttribute(\"aria-valuetext\", N + (N === 1 ? \" harmonic\" : \" harmonics\"));\n    // spectrum\n    sx.setTransform(dpr, 0, 0, dpr, 0, 0); sx.clearRect(0, 0, SW, SH);\n    var mx = 0.05; for (var n = 1; n <= MAXN; n++) mx = Math.max(mx, Math.hypot(a[n], b[n]));\n    var bw = SW / MAXN;\n    for (var m = 1; m <= MAXN; m++) {\n      var hgt = Math.hypot(a[m], b[m]) / mx * (SH - 18);\n      sx.globalAlpha = m <= N ? 1 : 0.35; sx.fillStyle = col[m <= N ? \"--ow-accent\" : \"--ow-muted\"];\n      var bx = (m - 1) * bw + bw * 0.18, bww = Math.max(2, bw * 0.64), top = SH - 16 - Math.max(any ? 1.5 : 0, hgt);\n      sx.beginPath(); if (sx.roundRect) sx.roundRect(bx, top, bww, SH - 16 - top, [2, 2, 0, 0]); else sx.rect(bx, top, bww, SH - 16 - top); sx.fill();\n    }\n    sx.globalAlpha = 1; sx.fillStyle = col[\"--ow-muted\"]; sx.font = \"11px \" + getComputedStyle(root).getPropertyValue(\"--ow-mono\");\n    [1, 10, 20, 30].forEach(function (m) { var t = String(m), tw = sx.measureText(t).width; sx.fillText(t, Math.min(SW - tw, Math.max(0, (m - 0.5) * bw - tw / 2)), SH - 2); });\n  }\n  var drawing = false, lastI = -1, lastV = 0;\n  function at(e) { var r = dc.getBoundingClientRect(); return [Math.max(0, Math.min(M - 1, Math.floor((e.clientX - r.left) / r.width * M))), Math.max(-1, Math.min(1, (H / 2 - (e.clientY - r.top) / r.height * H) / (H / 2 - 16)))]; }\n  function mark(i, v) {\n    if (lastI < 0) { y[i] = v; have[i] = 1; }\n    else { var d = i - lastI, st = d > 0 ? 1 : -1; for (var k = 0; k !== d + st; k += st) { var j = lastI + k; y[j] = lastV + (v - lastV) * (d ? k / d : 1); have[j] = 1; } }\n    lastI = i; lastV = v;\n  }\n  dc.addEventListener(\"pointerdown\", function (e) {\n    drawing = true; dc.setPointerCapture(e.pointerId); have.fill(0); lastI = -1; any = true; tip.style.opacity = 0;\n    var p = at(e); mark(p[0], p[1]); solve(); e.preventDefault();\n  });\n  dc.addEventListener(\"pointermove\", function (e) { if (!drawing) return; var list = e.getCoalescedEvents ? e.getCoalescedEvents() : [e]; (list.length ? list : [e]).forEach(function (ev) { var p = at(ev); mark(p[0], p[1]); }); solve(); });\n  [\"pointerup\", \"pointercancel\"].forEach(function (t) { dc.addEventListener(t, function () { drawing = false; lastI = -1; }); });\n  dc.addEventListener(\"keydown\", function (e) { if (e.key === \"e\" || e.key === \"E\") example(); else if (e.key === \"c\" || e.key === \"C\") clear(); });\n  slider.addEventListener(\"input\", function () { N = +slider.value; draw(); });\n  root.querySelector('[data-a=\"ex\"]').addEventListener(\"click\", example);\n  root.querySelector('[data-a=\"clear\"]').addEventListener(\"click\", clear);\n  new ResizeObserver(layout).observe(dc);\n  layout(); example(); tip.style.opacity = 1;\n})();\n</script>"
    },
    {
      "heading": "What people get wrong",
      "body": "- **\"Enough terms make it exact everywhere.\"** Not at a jump. The overshoot of about 9% stays for any finite number of terms [1].\n- **\"Every function has a Fourier series that works.\"** Smooth, well-behaved functions do; for many others the series does not converge to the function [2].\n- **\"Fourier series and the Fourier transform are the same thing.\"** The series is for shapes that repeat. The transform is the more general tool that also handles signals that do not [3].",
      "sources": [
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gibbs_phenomenon",
          "title": "Gibbs phenomenon (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "and this oscillation does not disappear but gets closer to the point so that the integral of the oscillation approaches zero."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_series",
          "title": "Fourier series (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "Well-behaved functions, for example smooth functions, have Fourier series that converge to the original function."
        },
        {
          "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fourier_series",
          "title": "Fourier series (Wikipedia)",
          "quote": "a more general tool that can even find the frequency information for functions that are not periodic"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
